    "citation": "Spektrafilm by Andrea Volpato and contributors; https://github.com/andreavolpato/spektrafilm . New calibration, not an upstream stock profile.",
    "datasource": "Kodak Ektachrome 160T Professional Film (EPT), publication E-144; SHA256 dab931a08934269f6e07993eddf25f67b9414842622ebc513ceac3a8f3fa8d53. Reproduce with scripts/bw_expansion/prepare_colour_film.py; axis calibration derived from the page by scripts/bw_expansion/extract_graphs.py; source points, assumptions and conditions: data/profile-sources/kodak-ektachrome-160t/recipe.json. PCHIP of the three plotted log-sensitivity traces; engine covers 380-780 nm, each trace is used only over its own plotted span and is unmeasured elsewhere. Relative shape only; the panel's E.N.D. density criterion is not an absolute speed. Not on the sheet. The dye panel is normalised to a visual neutral of 1.0 and plots no D-min, and the characteristic panel's minimum is a status-A reading, not a spectral curve. A flat 0.10 is assumed, within the 0.09-0.13 range the shipped positives carry. This is an assumption, not a measurement. Spectral adaptation parameters are not this stock's own: they are borrowed from kodak_ektachrome_100. Nearest shipped sibling: the same manufacturer's E-6 reversal family. It is a daylight stock where this one is tungsten, which is a known imperfection in the borrow. Density curves balanced against a rendered 5-stop grey ramp by scripts/bw_expansion/balance_against_ramp.py (upstream's correct_positive_curves_with_gray_ramp): density scale [0.9838, 1.0101, 0.9987], log-exposure shift [-0.0641, 0.0, 0.0392], data_trustability 0.5. Worst channel deviation from neutral across the ramp 35.8% before, 2.9% after. This correction is fitted against the engine, not measured from the datasheet."
  },
